    {
      q: 'When should a Christmas toy order be placed?',
      a: 'Work backwards from the shelf date: allow 20–35 days of sea freight, 7–10 days of clearance and inland delivery, and 15–25 days of production. A product on shelf by mid-November needs to ship from China by late September, which means a purchase order in July or August. That is also before the Chinese New Year congestion window, which is the single biggest cause of seasonal shipments arriving late.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What happens to production around Chinese New Year?',
      a: 'Most Chenghai factories close for one to three weeks and the workforce returns gradually, so the effective slowdown is longer than the official holiday. Freight capacity is also tight in the weeks before and after. For a spring or summer season, the safe rule is to have the goods on the water before the holiday rather than in production during it.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Do you have Christmas-specific products?',
      a: 'Yes — there is a Christmas-themed six-hole bubble stick in the catalogue, and several bubble machines and light-up items work for a holiday display with seasonal packaging. We can quote a printed holiday sleeve or box, but the print run has its own minimum, so tell us the quantity before you ask for custom artwork.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Can you hold stock for a later ship date?',
      a: 'We do not operate a storage programme for buyers — that would put your stock in our warehouse with no certainty for either side. What we can do is agree a production slot so the goods are made close to the ship date, which is the part that actually matters for cash flow. Discuss the timing before the order, not after.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Which seasons actually work for these products?',
      a: 'Bubble and water toys peak in late spring and summer, makeup and gift cases peak in Q4, and light-up items work across Q4 and Halloween. Easter is a smaller window but a real one for bubble and craft items. The mistake is ordering a summer item in April for a June promotion — the production window has already gone.',
    },
